## MCP servers

<!-- Delete this whole section if you use none. -->

| Server | Purpose | Operation |
|---|---|---|
| `vault` | Knowledge base (see above) | `<PATH>` — HTTP daemon `http://127.0.0.1:8765/mcp` |
| `<tracker>` | Tickets + wiki | `<PATH>` — HTTP daemon |
| `<db>` | Databases | `<PATH>` — stdio |
| `<git>` | Git / forge workflow | `<PATH>` — stdio |

**Daemon architecture:** exactly **one** long-lived container per server for all Claude instances
(one process = no lock collisions). Started via `<repo>/scripts/ensure-up.sh`, idempotent, wired
as a `SessionStart` hook.

**Careful:** the daemons run via `docker run` from `ensure-up.sh` — a `docker-compose.yml` in the
repo is **not** what is running. Changes to mounts/envs go into `ensure-up.sh` and only take
effect after `docker rm -f <name>` plus a fresh `ensure-up.sh`, because the script does not
recreate a running container.

**Self-healing — orphaned mount.**
*Symptom:* the server reports zero notes, a full re-index inserts nothing, reads of notes that
demonstrably exist return "not found" — while the server is healthy.
*Cause:* the bind mount survived a host-side re-sync and points at nothing.
*Fix, to be applied without asking* when the symptoms match:

```bash
docker exec <server> sh -c 'ls /vault | wc -l'   # 0 = orphaned
ls "<VAULT_PATH>" | wc -l                        # >0 = host is fine
docker restart <server> && sleep 4               # ensure-up.sh is NOT enough
```

Verify afterwards with a re-index and a status check. If `/vault` is still empty, escalate to me.

